% Automatic External Defibrillators: LCD L33690 and its Policy Article
% A52458 (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes
% dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills)
% and states when a claim for a wearable defibrillator (K0606), a
% nonwearable one (E0617) or a replacement supply of the wearable one
% (K0607, K0608, K0609) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: "beneficiaries at high
% risk for sudden cardiac death (SCD)". The wearable defibrillator needs one
% of four criteria (a documented episode of ventricular fibrillation or a
% sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia; a familial or inherited high-risk
% condition; a prior myocardial infarction or a dilated cardiomyopathy with
% an ejection fraction of 0.35 or less; an implanted defibrillator that
% requires explantation). The nonwearable one needs one of eight conditions
% (A) with implantation surgery contraindicated (B), or an implanted
% defibrillator that requires explantation (C).
%
% How the criteria are read. The conditions are what the record documents —
% the shared template "the medical record of B documents C" for the
% diagnoses (ventricular fibrillation, cardiac arrest due to ventricular
% fibrillation, myocardial infarction, coronary artery disease, dilated
% cardiomyopathy, ischemic and nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy, and the
% exclusions of condition 5), and measurements as numbers so that the
% thresholds are in the rules: the duration of a sustained tachyarrhythmia
% in seconds (30), the left ventricular ejection fraction as a fraction
% (0.35, 0.30 — the LCD writes it both ways), the NYHA class as a number (2,
% 3, 4 for II, III, IV), the dates of the myocardial infarction, of the
% electrophysiologic study and of the order (four weeks read as 28 days) and
% of the diagnosis of a nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy (three months
% read as 90 days). The familial or inherited conditions of high risk
% (wearable criterion 2, nonwearable condition 3) are documented conditions,
% the two the LCD names ("such as long QT syndrome or hypertrophic
% cardiomyopathy") listed as facts; another would be added with its
% evidence. Two criteria are clinical judgments — the judged template of
% dmepos.le, "the finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with
% who found it and why:
%   transient cause excluded (the dysrhythmia "may not be due to a transient
%   or reversible cause" — drug toxicity, severe hypoxia, acidosis,
%   hypokalemia, hypercalcemia, hyperkalemia, systemic infections,
%   myocarditis, the LCD's examples);
%   implantation surgery contraindicated (nonwearable criterion B).
% Condition 8 of the nonwearable list ("one of the previous criteria (1-7)
% and ... NYHA Class IV heart failure") is read as extending conditions 6
% and 7, the only ones that name a heart failure class, to class IV: the
% other conditions do not depend on the class. The wearable criterion's
% "not occur during the first 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction"
% and the nonwearable condition 2's "not associated with acute myocardial
% infarction" are one scenario fact, that the dysrhythmia occurred within
% 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction. That the treating practitioner
% "be experienced in the management of beneficiaries at risk for SCD" is an
% expectation, not a criterion, and is not modelled.
%
% The payment condition the policy adds (Policy Article A52458, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements"): "The diagnosis code that justifies
% the need for these items must be included on the claim" — a diagnosis code
% of the article's ICD-10 list. The list is data:
% sources/icd10/A52458_icd10_covered.csv, loaded as the table aed_icd10
% (columns code, group, article, description). The article's text does not
% say which HCPCS code each group serves; the groups differ only in the
% dilated cardiomyopathy codes (I42.0, I42.3-I42.9, I43, A18.84), present in
% group 2 and absent from group 1, and dilated cardiomyopathy is named in
% the wearable defibrillator's criterion 3: group 2 is read as the wearable
% defibrillator's (K0606 and its supplies K0607-K0609) and group 1 as the
% nonwearable one's (E0617) — a device of this model, stated as facts
% without provenance. Not modelled: the KX/GA/GZ and KF modifiers
% (billing); the coding of other defibrillators as A9270 and of E0617's
% supplies as A9999.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a condition* is a familial condition with a high risk of ventricular tachyarrhythmia.
    % the record
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia lasting *a number* seconds; undefined.
    the ventricular dysrhythmia of *a beneficiary* occurred within 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction; undefined.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of *a beneficiary* is *a number*; undefined.
    the NYHA heart failure class of *a beneficiary* is *a number*; undefined.
    the qualifying myocardial infarction of *a beneficiary* occurred on *a date*; undefined.
    the electrophysiologic study of *a beneficiary* was performed on *a date*; undefined.
    the electrophysiologic study of *a beneficiary* induced sustained ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation; undefined.
    the nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy of *a beneficiary* was diagnosed on *a date*; undefined.
    the previously implanted defibrillator of *a beneficiary* requires explantation; undefined.
    % the knowledge base
    *a condition* is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator.
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table aed_icd10.
    the ICD10 group of the article for code *a code* is *a group*.
    % derived
    *an item* is a wearable defibrillator.
    *an item* is a nonwearable defibrillator.
    *an item* is a wearable defibrillator supply.
    *a beneficiary* has a documented sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia.
    *a beneficiary* has a qualifying ventricular dysrhythmia.
    *a beneficiary* meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a nonwearable defibrillator *an item*.
    *a beneficiary* has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator *an item*.
    *a beneficiary* is free of the exclusions of condition 5.
    the claim diagnosis of *a beneficiary* is in the ICD10 group for *an item*.

% The article's ICD-10 list (sources/icd10/A52458_icd10_covered.csv): each
% row a code, its group, the article and the description.
the table aed_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52458_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base aeds includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base aeds includes:

LCD L33690 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33690".
the text of LCD L33690 is at "sources/lcd/L33690.txt".
Policy Article A52458 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52458".
the text of Policy Article A52458 is at "sources/article/A52458.txt".

% What the devices and the supplies are (the Policy Article's coding
% guidelines).
rule aeds_wearable with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Wearable, automatic, external defibrillators with integrated electrocardiogram analysis are coded using HCPCS code K0606":
an item is a wearable defibrillator
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "K0606".

rule aeds_nonwearable with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Non-wearable, automatic external defibrillators with integrated electrocardiogram capability are coded using HCPCS code E0617":
an item is a nonwearable defibrillator
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0617".

rule aeds_supply with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Replacement supplies and accessories for use with K0606 are coded using K0607, K0608, and K0609 as appropriate":
an item is a wearable defibrillator supply
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["K0607", "K0608", "K0609"].

% The exclusions of condition 5 (a prior myocardial infarction with an
% ejection fraction of 0.30 or less), as the record would document them;
% the time windows of the LCD ("within past 3 months", "within past month")
% are part of the condition's name.
cardiogenic shock is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Cardiogenic shock or symptomatic hypotension while in a stable baseline rhythm".
symptomatic hypotension in a stable baseline rhythm is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Cardiogenic shock or symptomatic hypotension while in a stable baseline rhythm".
coronary artery bypass graft within the past 3 months is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Had a coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) or percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) within past 3 months".
percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty within the past 3 months is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Had a coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) or percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) within past 3 months".
enzyme positive myocardial infarction within the past month is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Had an enzyme-positive MI within past month".
candidacy for coronary revascularization is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Clinical symptoms or findings that would make them a candidate for coronary revascularization".
irreversible brain damage from preexisting cerebral disease is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Irreversible brain damage from preexisting cerebral disease".
noncardiac disease with a likelihood of survival less than one year is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "Any disease, other than cardiac disease (e.g. cancer, uremia, liver failure), associated with a likelihood of survival less than one year".

% Which group of the article's ICD-10 list serves which code: a device of
% this model (see the header).
the ICD10 group of the article for code "E0617" is 1.
the ICD10 group of the article for code "K0606" is 2.
the ICD10 group of the article for code "K0607" is 2.
the ICD10 group of the article for code "K0608" is 2.
the ICD10 group of the article for code "K0609" is 2.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical
% equipment.
rule aeds_codes with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Automatic external defibrillators are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is aeds
    if the code is in ["E0617", "K0606", "K0607", "K0608", "K0609"].

section applicability is:

rule aeds_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Automatic external defibrillators are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is aeds.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The wearable defibrillator (K0606): one of criteria 1-4; its supplies
% under the same criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule aeds_wearable_covered with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A wearable defibrillator (K0606) is covered for beneficiaries if they meet one of the criteria (1-4), described below":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a wearable defibrillator
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator.

rule aeds_supplies_covered with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "Replacement supplies and accessories for use with K0606 are coded using K0607, K0608, and K0609 as appropriate":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a wearable defibrillator supply
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a wearable defibrillator
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator.

% Criterion 1: a documented ventricular fibrillation or sustained
% tachyarrhythmia, not of a transient cause, not in the first 48 hours of an
% acute myocardial infarction.
rule aeds_wearable_criterion_1 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A documented episode of ventricular fibrillation or a sustained, lasting 30 seconds or longer, ventricular tachyarrhythmia":
a beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator
    if the beneficiary has a qualifying ventricular dysrhythmia.

rule aeds_dysrhythmia_fibrillation with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "These dysrhythmias may be either spontaneous or induced during an electrophysiologic (EP) study, but may not be due to a transient or reversible cause and not occur during the first 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction":
a beneficiary has a qualifying ventricular dysrhythmia
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents ventricular fibrillation
    and the finding transient cause excluded about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the ventricular dysrhythmia of the beneficiary occurred within 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction.

rule aeds_dysrhythmia_tachyarrhythmia with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "These dysrhythmias may be either spontaneous or induced during an electrophysiologic (EP) study, but may not be due to a transient or reversible cause and not occur during the first 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction":
a beneficiary has a qualifying ventricular dysrhythmia
    if the beneficiary has a documented sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia
    and the finding transient cause excluded about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the ventricular dysrhythmia of the beneficiary occurred within 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction.

rule aeds_sustained_tachyarrhythmia with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "a sustained, lasting 30 seconds or longer, ventricular tachyarrhythmia":
a beneficiary has a documented sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia lasting a number seconds
    and the number >= 30.

% Criterion 2: a familial or inherited condition of high risk, documented
% in the record; the LCD names two ("such as"), listed below.
rule aeds_wearable_criterion_2 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Familial or inherited conditions with a high risk of life-threatening ventricular tachyarrhythmia such as long QT syndrome or hypertrophic cardiomyopathy":
a beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a familial condition with a high risk of ventricular tachyarrhythmia.

long QT syndrome is a familial condition with a high risk of ventricular tachyarrhythmia,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "such as long QT syndrome or hypertrophic cardiomyopathy".
hypertrophic cardiomyopathy is a familial condition with a high risk of ventricular tachyarrhythmia,
    as stated in LCD L33690, confer "such as long QT syndrome or hypertrophic cardiomyopathy".

% Criterion 3: a prior myocardial infarction or a dilated cardiomyopathy,
% and an ejection fraction of 0.35 or less.
rule aeds_wearable_criterion_3 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Either documented prior myocardial infarction or dilated cardiomyopathy and a measured left ventricular ejection fraction less than or equal to 0.35":
a beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is in [myocardial infarction, dilated cardiomyopathy]
    and the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of the beneficiary is a number
    and the number <= 0.35.

% Criterion 4: explantation.
rule aeds_wearable_criterion_4 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A previously implanted defibrillator now requires explantation":
a beneficiary meets a criterion for a wearable defibrillator
    if the previously implanted defibrillator of the beneficiary requires explantation.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The nonwearable defibrillator (E0617): (A) one of conditions 1-8 and (B)
% implantation surgery contraindicated, or (C) explantation.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule aeds_nonwearable_covered with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A nonwearable automatic defibrillator (E0617) is covered for beneficiaries in two circumstances. They meet either (1) both criteria A and B or (2) criteria C, described below":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a nonwearable defibrillator
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a nonwearable defibrillator the item.

rule aeds_nonwearable_a_and_b with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Implantation surgery is contraindicated":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator the item
    and the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about the beneficiary is established.

rule aeds_nonwearable_c with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A previously implanted defibrillator now requires explantation":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the previously implanted defibrillator of the beneficiary requires explantation.

% Condition 1: a cardiac arrest due to ventricular fibrillation.
rule aeds_condition_1 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A documented episode of cardiac arrest due to ventricular fibrillation, not due to a transient or reversible cause":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents cardiac arrest due to ventricular fibrillation
    and the finding transient cause excluded about the beneficiary is established.

% Condition 2: a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia.
rule aeds_condition_2 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "A sustained, lasting 30 seconds or longer, ventricular tachyarrhythmia, either spontaneous or induced during an electrophysiologic (EP) study, not associated with acute myocardial infarction, and not due to a transient or reversible cause":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a documented sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia
    and the finding transient cause excluded about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the ventricular dysrhythmia of the beneficiary occurred within 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction.

% Condition 3: a familial or inherited condition of high risk, documented.
rule aeds_condition_3 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Familial or inherited conditions with a high risk of life-threatening ventricular tachyarrythmias such as long QT syndrome or hypertrophic cardiomyopathy":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a familial condition with a high risk of ventricular tachyarrhythmia.

% Condition 4: coronary artery disease with a prior myocardial infarction,
% an ejection fraction of 0.35 or less, and an inducible tachycardia or
% fibrillation at an electrophysiologic study; the infarction more than four
% weeks (28 days) before the prescription (the order), the study more than
% four weeks after the infarction.
rule aeds_condition_4 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Coronary artery disease with a documented prior myocardial infarction with a measured left ventricular ejection fraction less than or equal to 0.35, and inducible, sustained ventricular tachycardia (VT) or ventricular fibrillation (VF) during an EP study":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents coronary artery disease
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents myocardial infarction
    and the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of the beneficiary is a number
    and the number <= 0.35
    and the electrophysiologic study of the beneficiary induced sustained ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation
    and the qualifying myocardial infarction of the beneficiary occurred on a date
    and the order for the item is dated an other date
    and the other date is an other number days after the date
    and the other number > 28
    and the electrophysiologic study of the beneficiary was performed on a third date
    and the third date is a third number days after the date
    and the third number > 28.

% Condition 5: a prior myocardial infarction with an ejection fraction of
% 0.30 or less, none of the exclusions.
rule aeds_condition_5 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Documented prior myocardial infarction and a measured left ventricular ejection fraction less than or equal to 0.30":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents myocardial infarction
    and the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of the beneficiary is a number
    and the number <= 0.30
    and the beneficiary is free of the exclusions of condition 5.

rule aeds_condition_5_exclusions with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Beneficiaries must not have":
a beneficiary is free of the exclusions of condition 5
    if it is not the case that
        the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
        and the condition is an exclusion of condition 5 for a nonwearable defibrillator.

% Conditions 6 and 7: an ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy with a prior
% myocardial infarction, or a nonischemic one of more than three months (90
% days) at the order; heart failure of NYHA class II or III — or IV
% (condition 8); an ejection fraction of 0.35 or less.
rule aeds_condition_6 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Beneficiaries with ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy (IDCM), documented prior myocardial infarction (MI), New York Heart Association (NYHA) Class II and III heart failure":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents myocardial infarction
    and the NYHA heart failure class of the beneficiary is a number
    and the number is in [2, 3, 4]
    and the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of the beneficiary is an other number
    and the other number <= 0.35.

rule aeds_condition_7 with provenance LCD L33690,
        confer "Beneficiaries with nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy (NIDCM) > 3 months, NYHA Class II and III heart failure":
a beneficiary has a qualifying condition for a nonwearable defibrillator an item
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy
    and the nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy of the beneficiary was diagnosed on a date
    and the order for the item is dated an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number > 90
    and the NYHA heart failure class of the beneficiary is an other number
    and the other number is in [2, 3, 4]
    and the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of the beneficiary is a third number
    and the third number <= 0.35.

% Condition 8 is read into conditions 6 and 7 (class IV admitted); its
% passage: "Beneficiaries who meet one of the previous criteria (1-7) and
% have NYHA Class IV heart failure".

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment: a diagnosis code of the article's
% list, in the group of the item's code, on the claim.
rule aeds_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is aeds
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the claim diagnosis of the beneficiary is in the ICD10 group for the item.

rule aeds_diagnosis_group with provenance Policy Article A52458,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the claim diagnosis of a beneficiary is in the ICD10 group for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the ICD10 group of the article for code the code is a group
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is an other code
    and ICD10 code the other code is in group the group of article "A52458" as a description under table aed_icd10.
